1
00:00:00,103 --> 00:00:06,474
Taking Over a Team My predecessor left a detailed handover A successor

2
00:00:06,645 --> 00:00:12,421
he warned should sift useful routines from wasteful ones The forthcoming project

3
00:00:12,434 --> 00:00:17,895
required us to marshal resources lengthen testing and terminate an outdated arrangement

4
00:00:18,803 --> 00:00:23,711
I asked colleagues to affirm what worked A senior employee was insistent

5
00:00:23,724 --> 00:00:29,263
that nothing change but we examined evidence I learnt to shoulder responsibility

6
00:00:29,276 --> 00:00:34,960
without claiming exclusive wisdom A mature manager should engage with criticism rather

7
00:00:34,974 --> 00:00:41,092
than expect obedient agreement Leadership involves succession as well as personal performance

8
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:46,013
A clear handover helps the next person understand a decision and revise

9
00:00:46,026 --> 00:00:49,592
it thoughtfully when conditions diverge from earlier expectations
